# Line endings: every text file is stored and checked out with Unix line endings (LF), on every computer,
# whatever git's own settings say. Without this, git on Windows may turn them into Windows ones (CRLF),
# and files end up mixing the two. Git decides by itself which files are text.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Spotify's logo files: never changed by git in any way.
*.svg -text
